      {
        "scene": "options",
        "beat": 1,
        "previousSay": "Now remove the insufficient-evidence candidate from our fixed-score miniature. The remaining probabilities renormalize even though their underlying scores stay unchanged. That illustrates dependence on the answer set. Keep no-match cases in your evaluation, and provide an explicit review or abstention choice when the application needs one."
      },
      {
        "scene": "options",
        "beat": 2,
        "previousSay": "Multiple questions also need isolation. An attention mask alone cannot isolate packed questions through recurrent state. A compatible implementation can continue separate question rows from one shared state cache. Add an unrelated question, or change its options, and check that the original question scores stay consistent within numerical tolerance. Shared state prefill does not mean every question runs in one accelerator pass."
      },
      {
        "scene": "release",
        "beat": 4,
        "previousSay": "That gives point six eight confidence. It clears point six five and enters the test investigation queue. Equality would also pass this gate. The queue gets a ticket to investigate. Rotating a credential or closing an incident needs a separate grant. Neither permission came back with the letter A."
      }
    ]
  },
